WEBVTT


00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.680
Add fabulous texture to
your knitting with bobbles.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.330
If you can put needles
in hold, you can do this.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.130
The idea behind bobbles is
partial knitting or bridging.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.430
Keep only the bobble stitches in work.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.510
Knit a few rows, hang the bobble.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.160
Rinse and repeat.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.650
We found some tricks for making
these neat without any extra fuss.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.150
The goal is to knit only one garment
row while we're  adding our bobbles.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.050
With the carriage on the
right, put needles into hold,

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.150
set the carriage to hold.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.610
It will stay in, hold
through the whole process.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.990
Knit to the left, across
the needles in work.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.810
Wrap the first needle.

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:53.790
Keeping the three bobble
needles in working position,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.920
put the remaining needles in hold.

00:00:57.315 --> 00:01:00.075
As you can see only
three needles are work.

00:01:01.485 --> 00:01:07.275
Knit five rows or an odd number of rows
ending with the carriage on the right.

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:12.975
Wrap that needle to the right.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.060
Pick up the stitches from the
first row of the bobble and

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.039
hang them on the bobble needles.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:48.240
Put the next set of needles into
working position and knit to the

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.580
left across all of those needles.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.210
This completes your first bobble.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.039
Closes up those stitches and you're
set up for your next sequence.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.590
Put all but the next three
bobble needles into hold.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.560
These three will be the second bobble.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:15.329
Wrap the needle on the left, knit
five rows ending on the right.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.880
Wrap the right needle.

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:30.705
Pick up the three stitches and hang
that bobble from the first row.

00:02:36.495 --> 00:02:39.315
Put the next set of needles
into working position.

00:02:40.695 --> 00:02:41.835
Knit across.

00:02:44.355 --> 00:02:48.525
You've completed the second bobble
and you're in position to create

00:02:48.525 --> 00:02:50.385
the next and the next and the next.

00:02:52.035 --> 00:02:53.385
Now here are the tricks.

00:02:54.105 --> 00:02:57.614
You'll position the carriage
correctly by knitting an odd

00:02:57.614 --> 00:02:59.595
number of rows for the bobble.

00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:01.454
In my case, five.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.685
Wrapping on each side, prevents holes.

00:03:14.415 --> 00:03:19.155
Picking up the first row of stitches
gives that bobble the desired dimension.

00:03:31.415 --> 00:03:37.035
As you can see in this example, only
one row was knit, keeping the row

00:03:37.035 --> 00:03:39.195
count, correct for the garment piece.

